Unabomber's manifesto.  However:

Does the above posting imply that the capitalist economy is a form of
artificial life, with the web adding a brain to it, i.e. artificial
intelligence?

Are memes (see alt.memetics) a new form of life?  Are they going to supplant
genetic life?

Should we adapt our terminology or at least our thinking concerning memetic
life and intelligence, consider it 'natural' and encourage it?  OR

Should genetic life rebel against this 'parasite' lifeform, and if so, what
constitutes the correct level of memetic evolution for humans, since we
require a lot of memes to survive?  How would this 'eating of the tree of
knowledge' be regulated?

Is _money_ one of the neuro-transmitters of the 'body of society' described
above?  Are the values that are registered in terms of monetary worth
serving the memetic or the genetic life forms?  Lastly:

With biotech will the genetic and memetic lifeforms mate to produce a hybrid
lifeform, thereby eliminating any cross-purposes of genetic and memetic
life?

